    "https://www.lec.edu/tuition-and-fees": {
      "title": "Tuition & Fees",
      "description": "Tuition & Fees | Lake Erie College top of page Skip to Main Content Search Apply Give VISIT Make a Payment LEO More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Menu Tuition and Payments Tuition and Fees at Lake Erie College At Lake Erie College, we’re committed to transparency when it comes to the cost of your education. Our Tuition and Fees page provides a clear breakdown of expenses so you can plan confidently for your college experience. From tuition rates and housing costs to meal plans and general fees, you’ll find all the information you need to understand your investment in a Lake Erie College education.​ ​ A college education is an important investment, but represents a major expense in most families' budgets. At Lake Erie College, we are committed to helping students find the means to afford a quality private education. ​ ​ ​ ​ Payment Options Online with Credit Card or ACH Payments: ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ NEW STUDENT DEPOSIT LINK Current Student Payment Other Payments In Person The Office of the Bursar is open Monday–Friday, 8:30 AM–4:30 PM for in-person payments. ​ Check Mail payments to: Office of the Bursar Lake Erie College 391 West Washington Street Painesville, OH 44077 Payment Deadlines Summer: Tuition payments due May 26 Fall: Tuition payments due August 24 Spring: Tuition payments due January 11 ​ ​​​ ​ Payment Plan Option Payment plans will be available on Transact each semester. Enrollment fee: $30 per plan ​ Fall Semester First day to enroll: July 1 Installments: 5 (July 15–Nov 15) Last day to enroll: Sept 10 Installments: 3 (Sept 15–Nov 15) Spring Semester First day to enroll: Nov 15 Installments: 5 (Dec 15–Apr 15) Last day to enroll: Feb 10 Installments: 3 (Feb 15–Apr 15) International students experiencing issues accessing the online payment page may contact bursar@lec.edu for assistance. Payment helpful links to Tailor your education experience Housing & Dining Apply Schedule a Visit to Campus Student Account Info Pamphlet Tuition and Fees Housing Meal Plans Summer Pricing Refund Schedule 2026-2027 Undergraduate tuition and fees Full-Time Undergraduate (12-18 credit hours per semester) ​ Annual Tuition: $38,950 General Fees (per semester): $1,000 Books and Supplies (estimated, per semester): $1,250 ​ Part-Time Undergraduate Tuition (per credit hour): $1,300 General College Fee (per credit hour): $75 ​ 2026-2027 graduate tuition and fees Master's Programs Master of Education (M.Ed.): $550 per credit hour Master of Business Administration (MBA): $750 per credit hour Master of Professional Studies (MPS): $750 per credit hour ​ Physician Assistant (PA) Tuition (per semester): Per Semester (Cohort Starting May 2027): $958 per credit hour ​ 2026-2027 Additional fees​ International Application Processing Fee: $200 Continuing International Student Fee: $150 per semester Academic Program Abroad Fee: Varies Audit: $50 per credit hour Graduation Fee: $250 Late Registration Fee: $165 Late Payment Fee: $50 per month (max $200 per semester) Returned Check Fee: $30 Athletic Insurance Fee: $350 Study Tour Surcharge: Assessed per tour Transcript Fee: $10 Tuition Payment Plan: $30 per semester/term ​ 2026-2027 Equine Studies fees Student Horse Board - Limited Care Plus: $2,700 per semester Student Horse Board - Limited Care: $2,300 per semester ​ Andrews Hall, Fowler Hall, Ritter Hall Includes free laundry service. Double Occupancy Room - $2,970 per semester Single Occupancy Room - $4,550 per semester ​ Dickinson Hall Includes free laundry service. Double Occupancy Room - $3,275 per semester Single Occupancy Room - $4,700 per semester ​ ​ The Tower Apartments (Off campus) Includes free laundry service and central AC. Located at 30 S Park Place, Painesville, OH 44077. For inquiries about The Tower, please email tower@renewptr.com . ​ ​ Studio: $5,555 (semester) 2 Bed: $5,130 (semester) 3 Bed With Window: $4,865 (semester) Without Window: $4,495 (semester) 4 Bed With Window: $4,655 (semester) Without Window: $4,020 (semester) 5 Bed With Window: $4,335 (semester) Without Window: $3,595 (semester) 6 Bed With Window: $4,125 (semester) Without Window: $3,385 (semester) 8 Bed With Window: $3,810 (semester) Without Window: $3,175 (semester) Summer Rate $950​ Winter Break $55​ ​ * Residential Meal Plan Required with College Housing. Students living on campus are required to select either Meal Plan 1 or Meal Plan 2. Students living at the Tower must choose Meal Plan 1, 2, or 3. ​ * The Tower Apartments are managed by Renew Partners. Through this unique partnership with Lake Erie College, upperclass students can fulfill their residency requirements for the College. However, the Towers are not considered to be \"on-campus\" housing, and Tower residents are not eligible for the LEC Residential Grant. In addition, rental payments are made directly to Renew Partners, as with any off-campus accommodation. ​ Meal Plan 1 $3,950 per Semester 345 Meal Swipes per Semester $200 Storm Dollars ​ Meal Plan 2 $3,600 per Semester 250 Meal Swipes per Semester $150 Storm Dollars​ ​ Meal Plan 3 $1,600 per Semester 100 Meal Swipes per Semester $100 Storm Dollars ​ Commuter Meal Plan $400 per Semester 25 Meal Swipes per Semester $75 Storm Dollars ​ *All students, including commuters, must have a meal plan. *Regardless of whether students live on or off campus, all student-athletes are required to have Meal Plan 1, 2, or 3. *Storm Dollars, which are included in every meal plan, cannot be used to purchase Bookstore Gift Cards. *All Storm Dollars expire on the last day of finals each spring semester. Unused meals expire at the end of each semester. *Other fees may apply. All prices are subject to change. 2026 Undergraduate Summer Tuition: Tuition (per credit hour): $499 2026 Graduate Summer Tuition: Master of Education (M.Ed.): $550 per credit hour Master of Business Administration (MBA): $750 per credit hour Master of Professional Studies (MPS): $750 per credit hour ​ 2026 Housing Summer Pricing: The Tower: $950 ​ 2026 Summer Semester Tuition will be refunded according to the following schedule: Session E (13-week course) May 11 - 100% May 12 - 80% May 13 - 0% ​ Session D (7-week course) May 26 - 100% May 27 - 80% May 28 - 0% ​ ****After May 28, no refunds will be issued. 2026 Fall Semester Tuition will be refunded according to the following schedule: Z - Schedule (Full Semester) During the first week: Aug. 24 through Aug 30......100% During the second week: Aug 31 through Sept. 6......80% During the third week: Sept. 7 through Sept. 13......60% ****After Sept 13th, no refunds will be issued X - Schedule (7-week courses) During the first week: Aug. 24 through Aug 30......100% During the second week: Aug 31 through Sept. 6......80% ****After Sept 7th, no refunds will be issued Y - Schedule (7-week courses) During the first week: Oct. 12 through Oct. 18......100% During the second week: Oct. 19 through Oct. 25......80% ****After Oct. 25th, no refunds will be issued Refunds for room and board are as follows: Prior to Aug. 24......100% During the first and second week: Aug. 24 through Sept. 6......80% During the third week: Sept. 7 through Sept. 13......60% ****After Sept. 13th, no refunds will be issued. Meal Plans are prorated during the first 3 weeks for the number of meals used at an average rate of $10 per meal. The student will also be charged for any Storm Dollars used. After the 3rd week of class, there will be no refunds for Meal Plans. ​ 2027 Spring Semester Tuition will be refunded according to the following schedule: Z - Schedule (Full Semester) During the first week: Jan. 11 through Jan. 17......100% During the second week: Jan. 18 through Jan. 24......80% During the third week: Jan. 25 through Jan 31......60% ****After Feb 1st, no refunds will be issued ​ X - Schedule (7-week courses) During the first week: Jan. 10 through Jan. 17......100% During the second week: Jan. 18 through Jan. 24......80% ****After Jan. 25th, no refunds will be issued ​ Y - Schedule (7-week courses) During the first week: Mar. 1 through Mar. 7......100% During the second week: Mar. 8 through Mar. 14......80% ****After Mar. 15th, no refunds will be issued Refunds for room and board are as follows: Prior to Jan. 11......100% During the 1st and 2nd weeks of the semester, Jan. 11 through Jan. 24 ......80% During the third week of the semester, Jan. 25 through Jan 31 .......60% **** After Feb. 1st, no refunds will be issued ​ ​ Meal Plans are prorated during the first 3 weeks for the number of meals used at an average rate of $10 per meal. The student will also be charged for any Storm Dollars used. After the 3rd week of class, there will be no refunds for Meal Plans. Visit Campus Overview Apply Request Info 391 W Washington St, Painesville, Ohio, 44077 440.375.7000 © 2026 Lake Erie College Campus Map Catalog and School Handbook Compliments and Complaints Consumer Information Make a Payment APPLY VISIT Give Lake Erie Online Close About History News and Announcements Faculty & Staff Board of Directors Accreditation Events Admissions Campus Tours Tuition & Fees Housing & Dining Financial Aid College Credit Plus (CCP) Office of Veterans and Military Service New Student Orientation Academics Academic Calendar Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Physician Assistant Program (PA) Study Abroad Partnerships & Pre-Professional Programs Professional Teacher Pathway Registrar Student Life Clubs & Organizations Tower Honors Program Career Development Career Closet Lincoln Learning Commons Campus Safety Non-Degree Programs Professional Development for Teachers Equine Studies Athletics Arts & Culture Alumni & Friends Parents & Family Careers Facilities Bookstore Campus Gear LAKE ERIE ONLINE bottom of page Double click the content to see meaning"
