    "https://www.lec.edu/about-lake-erie-college": {
      "title": "About | Lake Erie College",
      "description": "About | Lake Erie College top of page Skip to Main Content Search Apply Give VISIT Make a Payment LEO More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Menu ABOUT Lake Erie college Academic Video Our Mission and Vision Lake Erie College prepares students for meaningful careers through academic excellence and real world engagement. Self Discovery College is a transformative experience. Every academic course, collegiate sport or community program is designed to add to who you are. Creative Problem Solving Our students are equipped to solve problems to become productive contributors in an ever-changing global society. Personal Development We empower students to explore and develop strong personal attributes. Your personality is an illuminating piece of who you are! Ethical Balance We teach students to balance their personal and professional goals with the needs of those around them in an ethical way Our History Get to Know Us Lake Erie College has over 165 years of rich heritage and tradition that has served as the foundation for what our college is all about. We started as one of the first women's colleges in the Western Reserve area, and some of our earliest graduates became prominent leaders of the women's suffrage movement. It's that kind of passion and sense of responsibility that Lake Erie College has tried to instill in our students through our campus traditions and culture. Learn More Get to Know Us Some of the prominent buildings on Lake Erie College's campus in Painesville, Ohio, have been around since its conception. Most notably, College Hall was where some of the first classes were held when the college opened its Painesville location in 1859. Other buildings have come and gone since then, but our campus remains a source of inspiration and historical significance for both our students and the surrounding community. Read More Our Campus Accreditation Get to Know Us Lake Erie College is accredited by the Ohio Department of Higher Education and the Higher Learning Commission and is a member of the North Central Association of Colleges and Schools. Lake Erie College also holds accreditation from the British Horse Society (BHS). It is approved by the Accreditation Review Commission on Education for the Physician Assistant (ARC-PA) and The Council for the Accreditation of Educator Preparation (CAEP). Read More Visit Campus Overview Apply Request Info 391 W Washington St, Painesville, Ohio, 44077 440.375.7000 © 2026 Lake Erie College Campus Map Catalog and School Handbook Compliments and Complaints Consumer Information Make a Payment APPLY VISIT Give Lake Erie Online Close About History News and Announcements Faculty & Staff Board of Directors Accreditation Events Admissions Campus Tours Tuition & Fees Housing & Dining Financial Aid College Credit Plus (CCP) Office of Veterans and Military Service New Student Orientation Academics Academic Calendar Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Physician Assistant Program (PA) Study Abroad Partnerships & Pre-Professional Programs Professional Teacher Pathway Registrar Student Life Clubs & Organizations Tower Honors Program Career Development Career Closet Lincoln Learning Commons Campus Safety Non-Degree Programs Professional Development for Teachers Equine Studies Athletics Arts & Culture Alumni & Friends Parents & Family Careers Facilities Bookstore Campus Gear LAKE ERIE ONLINE bottom of page Double click the content to see meaning"
