    "https://www.lec.edu/housing-and-dining": {
      "title": "Housing & Dining",
      "description": "Housing & Dining | Lake Erie College top of page Skip to Main Content Search Apply Give VISIT Make a Payment LEO More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Menu Housing & Dining Housing & Dining at Lake Erie College At Lake Erie College, on-campus living is an integral part of the college experience. Students can choose from a variety of residence options — including traditional residence halls like Andrews, Ritter, Fowler, and Dickinson — each offering furnished rooms, community spaces, laundry facilities, and plenty of opportunities to connect with classmates. Upper-class students may also live in apartment-style housing options such as The Tower, which provide more independent living while still being closely connected to campus life. Residence Life promotes a supportive community through Resident Assistants and structured activities, helping students make the most of their time living on campus. ​ The Arthur S. Holden Center serves as a hub for daily meals, snacks, coffee, and social gatherings, featuring spots like Dickinson Dining Hall and the Storm Café. Meal plans are designed to fit different schedules and appetites, ensuring students have convenient access to nourishing food throughout the academic year. ​ ​ 2026 Fall Move-In Dates Soccer & Volleyball: August 7 Volleyball 10AM - 12PM Women’s Soccer 12PM - 2PM Men’s Soccer 2PM - 4PM Football & Cheer: August 10 Cheer 10AM - 12PM Football 1PM - 5PM Cross Country: August 14 10AM - 12PM Equestrian Students and Team Members: August 17 10AM - 1PM Freshman: August 20 12PM - 4PM Returning Students: August 22 9AM - 12PM ​ Move-In Info Housing Options Dining Menu Current Student Resources Make Payment Lincoln Learning Commons Career Development Housing Maintenance Request Dining Services & Information Andrews Hall Fowler Hall Ritter Hall Dickinson Hall The Tower Arthur S. Holden Center Andrews Hall Andrews, Ritter, and Fowler Halls are outfitted as a Lake Erie College student’s home away from home. Each residence hall contains a kitchenette, laundry facility, and a community area with a television. The rooms, furnished with two twin beds, dressers, and desks, contain approximately 144 square feet of living area. ​ Schedule a Visit Fowler Hall ​ Andrews, Ritter, and Fowler Halls are outfitted as a Lake Erie College student’s home away from home. Each residence hall contains a kitchenette, laundry facility, and a community area with a television. The rooms, furnished with two twin beds, dressers, and desks, contain approximately 144 square feet of living area. ​ ​ Schedule a Visit Ritter Hall​ Ritter Hall is outfitted as a Lake Erie College student’s home away from home. Each residence hall contains a kitchenette, laundry facility, and a community area with a television. The rooms, furnished with two twin beds, dressers, and desks, contain approximately 144 square feet of living area. ​ Schedule a Visit Dickinson Hall ​Tracy H. Dickinson Hall has a community kitchenette, laundry facilities, lounges, and 43 student rooms. This residence hall has triple and quad rooms furnished to be a student's home away from home. Connections for telephone and high-speed Internet access are provided in each room. ​ Schedule a Visit The Tower ​ Includes free laundry service and central AC. Located at 30 S Park Place, Painesville, OH 44077. For inquiries about The Tower, please email thetower@rhmrealestategroup.com . ​ The Tower Apartments are managed by Renew Partners. Through this unique partnership with Lake Erie College, upper-class students can fulfill their residency requirements for the College. However, the Towers are not considered to be \"on-campus\" housing and Tower residents are not eligible for the LEC Residential Grant. In addition, rental payments are made directly to Renew Partners, as with any off-campus accommodation. ​ Learn More About The Tower Arthur S. Holden Center The Holden Center offers a variety of amenities to support students throughout their day. Dickinson Dining Hall and the Storm Café provide two convenient locations for meals, coffee, and snacks, with semester menus available to view online. The Lake Erie College Bookstore is stocked with textbooks, school supplies, and official LEC gear. Lounge areas such as the Commuter Lounge and Storm Shelter offer comfortable spaces to relax, recharge, or connect with friends. For academic needs, students can take advantage of both quiet study areas and group-friendly spaces designed for collaboration. ​ View Dining Menu Housing Options Office of Financial Aid Visit Campus Overview Apply Request Info 391 W Washington St, Painesville, Ohio, 44077 440.375.7000 © 2026 Lake Erie College Campus Map Catalog and School Handbook Compliments and Complaints Consumer Information Make a Payment APPLY VISIT Give Lake Erie Online Close About History News and Announcements Faculty & Staff Board of Directors Accreditation Events Admissions Campus Tours Tuition & Fees Housing & Dining Financial Aid College Credit Plus (CCP) Office of Veterans and Military Service New Student Orientation Academics Academic Calendar Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Physician Assistant Program (PA) Study Abroad Partnerships & Pre-Professional Programs Professional Teacher Pathway Registrar Student Life Clubs & Organizations Tower Honors Program Career Development Career Closet Lincoln Learning Commons Campus Safety Non-Degree Programs Professional Development for Teachers Equine Studies Athletics Arts & Culture Alumni & Friends Parents & Family Careers Facilities Bookstore Campus Gear LAKE ERIE ONLINE bottom of page Double click the content to see meaning"
