    "https://www.lec.edu/college-credit-plus": {
      "title": "College Credit Plus (CCP)",
      "description": "College Credit Plus (CCP) | Lake Erie College top of page Skip to Main Content Search Apply Give VISIT Make a Payment LEO More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Menu College Credit Plus Lake Erie College's CCP program allows eligible students to earn high school and college credit that will appear on both their high school and college transcripts. ​ College Credit Plus (CCP) was established by Ohio law in September 2014, replacing the Post Secondary Enrollment Options (PSEO) program. Effective beginning with the 2015-2016 school year, CCP redefines \"alternative dual enrollment programs.\" For more information, visit the Ohio Department of Education. Ohio Department of Education. Lake Erie College offers CCP opportunities for students in traditional classroom settings (typically in-person).  Exceptions to this policy must be approved by the Dean of the division in which the course is housed as well as the Provost.  Courses offered through LEC's partnership with Rize are currently not available for CCP enrollment. ​ Lake Erie College offers two options for College Credit Plus: On-Campus Take college courses on the LEC campus. Dual Enrollment Take college courses at your high school with accredited teachers through our dual enrollment program. Speak with your guidance counselor to see if we are offering dual enrollment at your school. ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ helpful links to Tailor your education experience Contact us about College Credit Plus Apply Schedule a Visit to Campus Application Process Common Courses Course Equivalency FAQs Common CCP Courses CCP students can take any undergraduate courses for which they meet the prerequisites. Exceptions include physical education courses, individual lessons, and equestrian riding courses. Common courses include: ​ EN 101: Composition and Research EN 201: Advanced College Writing MT 109: Pre-Calculus I EC 201: Macroeconomics EC 202: Microeconomics CM 105: Public Speaking PS 101: General Psychology PO 110: American National Government *To participate in math courses through CCP, students must have successfully completed Algebra 2. ​ Course Content Disclaimer The content of courses under the College Credit Plus program may include mature subject matter, such as graphic, explicit, violent, or sexual material. This content will not be modified based on a student's participation in the CCP program, regardless of the location of course instruction. ​ ​ View Catalog College Credit Plus (CCP) Who can participate in CCP? Any Ohio student in grades 7–12—public, private, or homeschooled (with required paperwork)—may participate in CCP. Does CCP cost anything? Most public school students have tuition and textbooks covered. Homeschooled or private school students may be responsible for textbooks or additional fees. Do CCP grades appear on both transcripts? Yes. Grades appear on both your high school transcript and your Lake Erie College transcript. Does CCP affect sports eligibility? Please check with your high school counselor or athletic association to confirm eligibility requirements. What if my high school’s spring break is different from the college’s spring break? Students must attend CCP courses at Lake Erie College even if their middle or high school is on break. Students are expected to follow the college’s academic calendar. Is transportation provided? Lake Erie College does not provide transportation for CCP students. However, we partner with LakeTran, which may be able to assist with transportation options. ​ Admissions What do I need to do to apply? Submit your application, your high school transcript, and a signed Mature Content Form. What GPA is required? A 3.0 GPA is preferred. Students below a 3.0 GPA may be required to complete a placement test for admission consideration. Is a placement test required? The placement test is required for students entering 7th, 8th, or 9th grade. It may also be required for students entering 10th, 11th, or 12th grade if they have a GPA below 3.0. When is the Intent to Participate form due? April 1 for the upcoming school year. Will there be an orientation? Yes. Accepted students will participate in a virtual orientation. Additional information will be provided upon acceptance. ​ Advising & Academics Are all courses available through CCP? CCP students may enroll in undergraduate courses for which they meet the prerequisites. Exceptions include physical education courses, individual lessons, and equestrian riding courses. Where can I take CCP classes? Classes may be taken on campus, online, or at your high school (if your district permits). Students may take one online course per semester. Can I take summer courses? Yes. Summer courses count toward your annual CCP credit limit. How many courses can I take each year? Ohio limits the combined total of high school and college credits to 30 credit hours per academic year. Your high school guidance counselor can help you plan accordingly. What if I do not meet the prerequisites? You must complete the required prerequisites before enrolling in the course. Can I take classes related to my future major? Yes, as long as you meet the prerequisites. Many students begin with general education courses. What happens if I fail or withdraw from a course? Failing grades remain on both transcripts. Withdrawals appear as a “W” and may have financial consequences if deadlines have passed. Can my parents see my grades? Only with your permission. FERPA protects student privacy. Will CCP credits transfer to other colleges? In most cases, yes; however, each college or university sets its own transfer policies. Students should consult with future college advisors. How do I get textbooks? Textbooks can be picked up at the bookstore during the first week of the semester and must be returned by finals week. Do I need to meet with an advisor every semester? Yes. Your advisor will help you stay on track, meet requirements, and register for courses properly. Are CCP grades part of my permanent college record? Yes. As a CCP student, you are establishing a permanent college transcript. The grades you earn in the program are very important. You will be required to submit this transcript to any college or university to which you apply in the future. ​ High School Subject Equivalencies Below is a general guide showing how high school subject areas may align with Lake Erie College courses. ​ English EN 101 – College Writing I EN 201 – College Writing II Math MT 109 – Pre-Calculus I MT 110 – Pre-Calculus II All upper-level math courses may also qualify Science BI 100 – Biology Concepts CH 100 – Chemistry in Context ES 104 – Introduction to Environmental Science PC 106 – Introduction to Physical Science Social Studies Any course with the prefix: HI, SO, PS, EC, or PO Government PO 110 – American National Government Economics EC 101 – Macroeconomics EC 102 – Microeconomics Fine Arts Any course with the prefix: AT, MU, or TH Foreign Language Italian Spanish Electives Any other course, provided prerequisites are met Important: Students should meet with their high school guidance counselor to ensure they are fulfilling all high school graduation requirements. ​ View Catalog Application Process for CCP Students Step 1: Attend a High School CCP Information Session Step 2: Complete the Intent to Participate Form. Return the completed form to your high school by April 1 ​ Step 3: File a CCP Application to Lake Erie College by June 1 ​ Step 4: Submit High School Transcript​ Students must be attending full-time at a high school in the State of Ohio or state-approved homeschool​ ​ Step 5: Determine Eligibility and Placement​​ Minimum GPA: 3.0 preferred Placement tests may be requested to determine eligibility All applications will undergo a thorough review to verify that students have demonstrated their readiness for college coursework. ​ Step 6: Wait for Admittance Decision! Step 7: Once accepted, orientation information will be emailed to you once it is available to students. For questions about orientation, please get in touch by emailing ccpinfo@lec.edu Step 8: Schedule an Appointment with an Academic Advisor to select classes and register (Fall Deadline to Register: June 1, Spring Deadline to Register: January 1) ​ ​ APPLY Visit Campus Overview Apply Request Info 391 W Washington St, Painesville, Ohio, 44077 440.375.7000 © 2026 Lake Erie College Campus Map Catalog and School Handbook Compliments and Complaints Consumer Information Make a Payment APPLY VISIT Give Lake Erie Online Close About History News and Announcements Faculty & Staff Board of Directors Accreditation Events Admissions Campus Tours Tuition & Fees Housing & Dining Financial Aid College Credit Plus (CCP) Office of Veterans and Military Service New Student Orientation Academics Academic Calendar Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Physician Assistant Program (PA) Study Abroad Partnerships & Pre-Professional Programs Professional Teacher Pathway Registrar Student Life Clubs & Organizations Tower Honors Program Career Development Career Closet Lincoln Learning Commons Campus Safety Non-Degree Programs Professional Development for Teachers Equine Studies Athletics Arts & Culture Alumni & Friends Parents & Family Careers Facilities Bookstore Campus Gear LAKE ERIE ONLINE bottom of page Double click the content to see meaning"
    },
