    "https://www.lec.edu/registrars-office": {
      "title": "Registrar",
      "description": "Registrar | Lake Erie College top of page Skip to Main Content Search Apply Give VISIT Make a Payment LEO More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Menu registrar's office helpful links to Tailor your education experience Housing & Dining Apply Schedule a Visit to Campus International Student Policies TRANSCRIPT & VERIFICATION SERVICES NOTRE DAME COLLEGE TRANSCRIPTS COMMENCEMENT CEREMONY Degree and Enrollment Verification Requests Lake Erie College is the institution of record for Notre Dame College transcripts following the institution's closure after the spring 2024 semester. Official transcripts can be requested through the National Student Clearinghouse website . ​ Lake Erie College has authorized the National Student Clearinghouse to provide all enrollment and degree verifications. The National Student Clearinghouse can be contacted at: ​ Web: www.degreeverify.org ​ Mail: National Student Clearinghouse ​ 2300 Dulles Station Boulevard, Suite 300 ​ Herndon, VA 20171 ​ Transcripts Official transcript requests can be made through the National Student Clearinghouse Website . The cost for an official transcript is $10.00 for each transcript. An additional service fee applies to orders through the National Student Clearinghouse. eTranscripts are only available through the National Student Clearinghouse option. ​ Current students may obtain an unofficial transcript from the student Portal, Lake Erie Online (LEO). Lake Erie College alumni and past students can request an unofficial transcript at no cost by clicking here , and it cannot be ordered through the National Student Clearinghouse. They are generated primarily for your own records and printed on plain white paper with no official college signature or seal. We cannot provide unofficial transcripts for Notre Dame College alumni and past students . ​ Transcripts are processed in the order of receipt. Normally, it takes 2-4 business days to process a request. However, it may take 5-7 business days for processing at certain times of the year, such as at the beginning or end of each semester. ​ Note: The Registrar's Office will not release transcripts, unofficial or official, unless the student has met all admission and financial obligations to the College, returned all library materials, athletic items, and paid applicable fines. ​ GRADUATION INFORMATION Lake Erie College welcomes graduates and their families. Please familiarize yourself with the information contained in this section and share it with others who may be accompanying you on this special day. We appreciate your understanding and cooperation as we celebrate this momentous occasion. ​ Lake Erie College welcomes graduates and their families. Please familiarize yourself with the information in this section and share it with others who may accompany you on this special day. We appreciate your understanding and cooperation as we celebrate this momentous occasion. Click here for commencement ceremony details.​ ​ Tickets You must have tickets for the ceremony. Graduates must report to the facility an hour before the ceremony and stay there until the ceremony procession begins. Rehearsal Information Rehearsal is mandatory and will occur before the ceremony. We will email the rehearsal dates and times along with your graduation confirmation. If you do not attend the rehearsal, we will not allow you to participate in the ceremony. The seating chart will be based on rehearsal attendance and will not change after rehearsal. We will run through the entire ceremony during rehearsal, so you will cross the stage when your name gets called. ​ Not Participating? Notify the Registrar's Office if you know you will not participate in the graduation ceremony. ​ Appropriate Attire for Commencement Take your cap and gown out of the bag and hang it on a hanger a few days before the ceremony to let the wrinkles relax. To ensure a neat appearance, steam or iron your gown with a WARM iron (not hot). Don't have a steamer or iron? Hang your gown in the bathroom, and the steam from the shower should reduce wrinkles! Wear dresses or dress pants with a blouse and clean dress shoes. Flip-flops are inappropriate footwear, and we suggest avoiding high heels. ​ Graduation Regalia All graduating students participating in the ceremony must order graduation regalia (cap and gown). Submit your regalia order with the graduation form to the Registrar's Office. Orders placed after the submitted regalia order may incur an additional $10.00 late fee to cover special processing and shipping costs. The Registrar’s Office will distribute all caps and gowns. Return your cap, gown, and hood to the designated location following the graduation ceremony. We will withhold your diploma and charge you for the cap and gown replacement cost if you fail to return it after the ceremony. ​ Billing & Transcripts Remember, we will not release your diploma until you have fully paid your account. Transcripts may be requested at www.getmytranscript.com Note that your graduation statement will not appear on the transcript until after graduation. For other graduation-related questions, contact the Registrar's Office. All graduating students must pay the Graduation Fee, even if they choose not to participate in Commencement. While part of the fee covers auditing your record and procuring your diploma, the primary purpose is to maintain your record securely from now on. ​ Frequently Asked Questions Have more questions? FAQs can be answered here . ​ GRADUATION APPLICATION All students must apply to graduate. Submit graduation applications for spring and summer graduation by October 1st and for fall graduation by April 1st . The $250.00 graduation fee will be added to your account. If you have questions about graduation applications or deadlines, please call the Registrar's Office at (440) 375-7010. ​ GRADUATION APPLICATION Office of THE REGISTRAR Lauren Feola Interim Registrar Natasha Gaines Assistant Registrar Lyric Stancliff Academic Advisor Visit Campus Overview Apply Request Info 391 W Washington St, Painesville, Ohio, 44077 440.375.7000 © 2026 Lake Erie College Campus Map Catalog and School Handbook Compliments and Complaints Consumer Information Make a Payment APPLY VISIT Give Lake Erie Online Close About History News and Announcements Faculty & Staff Board of Directors Accreditation Events Admissions Campus Tours Tuition & Fees Housing & Dining Financial Aid College Credit Plus (CCP) Office of Veterans and Military Service New Student Orientation Academics Academic Calendar Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Physician Assistant Program (PA) Study Abroad Partnerships & Pre-Professional Programs Professional Teacher Pathway Registrar Student Life Clubs & Organizations Tower Honors Program Career Development Career Closet Lincoln Learning Commons Campus Safety Non-Degree Programs Professional Development for Teachers Equine Studies Athletics Arts & Culture Alumni & Friends Parents & Family Careers Facilities Bookstore Campus Gear LAKE ERIE ONLINE bottom of page Double click the content to see meaning"
    },
    "https://www.lec.edu/current-students": {
      "title": "Student Life",
      "description": "Student Life | Lake Erie College top of page Skip to Main Content Search Apply Give VISIT Make a Payment LEO More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Menu Student Life We're Here to Help Reality sets in pretty quickly. Who knew that Easy Mac catches on fire in the microwave if you forget to add enough water? Why does the Biology class start at 8 am on Monday? And laundry? Where does it all come from — do dirty socks reproduce in the basket? ​ College students just like you have walked these halls for over 160 years, and we're here to help you transition from a high school kid to a successful college graduate in no time. ​ Quick Links Financial Aid & Scholarships Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Partnerships & Accelerated Programs VETS Program Clubs & Organizations Tricks of the Trade First, you need a room, usually equipped with one or two friendly roommates and a cool resident assistant (RA) living just down the hall. Next, you need food. Easy Mac works in a pinch, but a well-stocked cafeteria and a few conveniently located cafes are a blessing, especially since you had to spend your pizza money on laundry soap last week. Mix in a 24/7 Security Department staffed by some pretty cool officers and now you can get down to learning in a safe place with the comforts of home. Things to Do All work and no play makes Jack and Jill jump over the moon with a dish. Or something along those lines. LEC offers an array of activities outside of the classroom to give your brain a break from the books. We have some pretty amazing clubs, sports, and organizations to help you have fun, stay fit, and find your tribe. An added bonus: employers look for extracurricular activities on resumes when they make hiring decisions. About Finding a Job Your years at LEC will include some amazing experiences. You begin as a teenager and graduate as an amazing version of yourself you only dreamed about. Your final college step is a leap into the workforce, landing the career of your dreams or at least grabbing the first rung on your way up the ladder. Our Office of Career Development specializes in helping you find that ladder and make the jump. Office of Student Affairs Jenn Miller, PHD Dean of Academic and Student Engagement Title IX Appeals Coordinator Tim Neary Academic Support Coordinator Title IX Deputy Coordinator Erika Ruedin Director of Future Educators Title IX Deputy Coordinator Visit Campus Overview Apply Request Info 391 W Washington St, Painesville, Ohio, 44077 440.375.7000 © 2026 Lake Erie College Campus Map Catalog and School Handbook Compliments and Complaints Consumer Information Make a Payment APPLY VISIT Give Lake Erie Online Close About History News and Announcements Faculty & Staff Board of Directors Accreditation Events Admissions Campus Tours Tuition & Fees Housing & Dining Financial Aid College Credit Plus (CCP) Office of Veterans and Military Service New Student Orientation Academics Academic Calendar Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Physician Assistant Program (PA) Study Abroad Partnerships & Pre-Professional Programs Professional Teacher Pathway Registrar Student Life Clubs & Organizations Tower Honors Program Career Development Career Closet Lincoln Learning Commons Campus Safety Non-Degree Programs Professional Development for Teachers Equine Studies Athletics Arts & Culture Alumni & Friends Parents & Family Careers Facilities Bookstore Campus Gear LAKE ERIE ONLINE bottom of page Double click the content to see meaning"
    },
    "https://www.lec.edu/student-organizations-and-clubs": {
      "title": "Clubs & Organizations",
      "description": "Clubs & Organizations | Lake Erie College top of page Skip to Main Content Search Apply Give VISIT Make a Payment LEO More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Menu Student Organizations and clubs Get Involved at Lake Erie College College is about more than earning a degree, it’s about discovering your passions, building connections, and preparing for your future. At Lake Erie College, our student organizations and clubs are open to everyone. Whether you want to explore a new interest, connect with others who share your enthusiasm, or simply try something different, there’s a place for you here. Get involved, make memories, and enhance your college experience—no prior experience required, just bring your curiosity and energy! ​ Don’t See a Club That Fits Your Interests? Start One! ​Creating a new student organization at Lake Erie College is simple. ​ Here’s what you’ll need: A Few Interested Students: Gather a small group of peers who share your vision. An Advisor: Find a faculty member willing to support your organization. An Application Form: Complete the required form to begin the approval process. ​ Once your materials are submitted, the Student Government Association (SGA) will review your proposal and vote on your club’s approval. ​ CURRENT ORGANIZATION & CLUB NAMES Creative Writing Club Faculty Advisor Amy Kesegich cwc@lec.edu View More CRU Faculty Advisor Vanessa Majewski cru@lec.edu View More Entomology Club Faculty Advisor Cari Ritzenthaler critzenthaler@lec.edu View More Lake Erie Book Club Faculty Advisor Jennifer Swartz-Levine bookclub@lec.edu View More Lake Erie College Sustainability Group Faculty Advisor Megan Acord sustainability@lec.edu View More Lake Erie College Tomorrow's Teachers Faculty Advisor Gregory Rothwell and Amy Markijohn tomorrowsteachers@lec.edu View More Laddies Legacy Faculty Advisor Laura Stockhaus laddieslegacy@lec.edu View More LeadHERship Society Faculty Advisor Jennifer Swartz-Levine leadherhsip@lec.edu View More Italian Culture Club Faculty Advisor Paola Basile italianclub@lec.edu View More STEMM Scholars Faculty Advisor Dr.  Jonathan Tedesco jtedesco@lec.edu View More Pre-Healthcare Club Faculty Advisor Dr. Jonathan Tedesco pre-healthcareclub@lec.edu View More Pre-Veterinary Club Faculty Advisor Dr. Michael Cinotti prevet@lec.edu View More Student Athletic Advisory Committee ​ SAAC saac@lec.edu View More Student Government Association Faculty Advisor Dr. Jenn Miller sga@lec.edu View More United Through Marketing Faculty Advisor Kathy Skledar utmc@lec.edu View More Visit Campus Overview Apply Request Info 391 W Washington St, Painesville, Ohio, 44077 440.375.7000 © 2026 Lake Erie College Campus Map Catalog and School Handbook Compliments and Complaints Consumer Information Make a Payment APPLY VISIT Give Lake Erie Online Close About History News and Announcements Faculty & Staff Board of Directors Accreditation Events Admissions Campus Tours Tuition & Fees Housing & Dining Financial Aid College Credit Plus (CCP) Office of Veterans and Military Service New Student Orientation Academics Academic Calendar Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Physician Assistant Program (PA) Study Abroad Partnerships & Pre-Professional Programs Professional Teacher Pathway Registrar Student Life Clubs & Organizations Tower Honors Program Career Development Career Closet Lincoln Learning Commons Campus Safety Non-Degree Programs Professional Development for Teachers Equine Studies Athletics Arts & Culture Alumni & Friends Parents & Family Careers Facilities Bookstore Campus Gear LAKE ERIE ONLINE bottom of page Double click the content to see meaning"
